From 0c4a48560db0471c6b53b2b406ee46527d50abbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:00:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] kosmickrisp: apply Metal rate maps to subsampled FDM
 passes (fdm_rate)

With MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=fdm,fdm_rate, keep a CPU copy of density map
uploads, build a cached MTLRasterizationRateMap from it (two samples per
map texel, per-axis maxima per layer) and set it on render passes whose
attachments are all subsampled, carrying it across the custom resolve
switch. Subsampled images and the density image get a parameter block
holding the map's physical sizes and Metal parameter data, and the root
table carries the active block's address. KK_FDM_DEBUG=1 logs map
creation and full-rate fallbacks.

FragCoord and subsampled sampling are not yet mapped, so output is not
correct with fdm_rate; without it nothing changes.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

